Cell["The old names, kept for one release and then removed", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2b41c4a9-15e8-1804-597e-ddf3a39d6b6e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The eleven retired names (ten functions and the ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<StimCircuit\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13ecd9ee-6506-67bb-4193-d0c80cb34d81"],
 " property) lived for one release in ",
 Cell["Deprecated.wl", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "6724c974-bdf1-27a5-0edb-e13e3b858d8f"],
 ", returning what they had returned and saying once per session what to use \
instead. That release is over: the file is gone, and so is the detector \
model's ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<StimString\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b52875c-0948-9ae8-5961-1f06a8e2e832"],
 ". An old property name now gets the same answer as any unknown one:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],

